# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the OPC-UA server with SecurityPolicy=None and
# anonymous access on 0.0.0.0:4840 then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the insecure endpoint is ALREADY LIVE when the agent starts (a do-nothing
#     agent must fail the discovery/anonymous-connect checks);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the python server cannot kill it.
#
# The fix edits the server script AND restarts the process. Because the running
# server keeps offering the None endpoint until it is restarted, the
# "edited the script but forgot to restart" case is genuinely detectable: the
# verifier queries the LIVE endpoint list, not the file.
